			"Message": "build(deps): bump @effect/platform from 0.95.0 to 0.96.0\n\nBumps [@effect/platform](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/tree/HEAD/packages/platform) from 0.95.0 to 0.96.0.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/main/packages/platform/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/commits/@effect/platform@0.96.0/packages/platform)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@effect/platform\"\n  dependency-version: 0.96.0\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "10158df01e1f01208bca2aa56b1ac698161f0f0c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-19T17:13:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Cocoon): update dependencies and enhance README branding\n\nThis commit performs routine dependency updates for the Cocoon extension host and improves the project documentation.\n\n### Dependency Updates\n- **Effect Framework**: Bumped `@effect/platform` (0.94.5 → 0.95.0), `@effect/platform-node` (0.104.1 → 0.105.0), and `effect` (3.19.19 → 3.20.0) to leverage latest performance improvements in the declarative services layer.\n- **Effect Extras**: Updated `@effect/experimental` (0.58.0 → 0.59.0), `@effect/language-service` (0.77.0 → 0.80.0), and `@effect/opentelemetry` (0.61.0 → 0.62.0).\n- **OpenTelemetry**: Updated SDK packages to latest stable versions including `sdk-trace-base` (2.6.0), `sdk-metrics` (2.5.1 → 2.6.0), and `sdk-trace-web` (2.5.1 → 2.6.0).\n- **Testing**: Upgraded `vitest` (4.0.18 → 4.1.0) and `@vitest/coverage-v8` (4.0.18 → 4.1.0) for improved test coverage reporting.\n- **Build**: Updated `esbuild` (0.27.3 → 0.27.4) and `@types/node` (25.3.3 → 25.5.0).\n\n### Documentation\n- Restructured README header table to include Land branding with direct link to Editor.Land, improving the integration visibility within the Land ecosystem.\n\nThese updates maintain the Cocoon extension host's compatibility with the latest Effect-TS stack and ensure optimal observability via OpenTelemetry.",
			"SHA": "5aac78f7878020e4619f35dcabef71e9f814ec8d"
		},
